.TH tuprovider-sftp n 0.1 tclutils
.SH "tuprovider::sftp \-\- SFTP provider"
.PP
An SFTP backend for the \fBtuprovider\fR interface, built on the OpenSSH \fBsftp\fR client run in batch mode (\fBsftp \-b\fR).
.PP
There is no pure\-Tcl SFTP client, so this adapter shells out to the system \fBsftp\fR binary: each operation runs a small batch script and its output is parsed. That keeps the dependency to something every SSH install already has, and inherits OpenSSH's authentication (keys, agent, \fBknown_hosts\fR) rather than reimplementing it.
.SS Load
.CS
tcl::tm::path add /path/to/tclutils/lib/tm
package require tclutils::tuprovider::sftp
.CE
.PP
Loading the package registers the \fBsftp\fR scheme with \fBtuprovider\fR.
.SS Open
.CS
set p [::tclutils::tuprovider open sftp sftp://user@host/pub \
        -identity ~/.ssh/id_ed25519]
.CE
.PP
The URL is \fBsftp://[user@]host[:port][/base]\fR. Options after it:
.IP \(bu
\fB\-identity FILE\fR  ssh private key (passed as \fB\-i\fR)
.IP \(bu
\fB\-port N\fR         port (overrides one given in the URL)
.IP \(bu
\fB\-sshopt {...}\fR   extra \fB\-o\fR options for sftp, repeatable, e.g. \fB\-sshopt {StrictHostKeyChecking=accept\-new}\fR
.IP \(bu
\fB\-batchcmd CMD\fR   override the sftp executable (default \fBsftp\fR)
.PP
Authentication is OpenSSH's: use a key via \fB\-identity\fR or an ssh\-agent. The host must be in \fBknown_hosts\fR (or use \fB\-sshopt {StrictHostKeyChecking=accept\-new}\fR to add it on first connect) \-\- because sftp runs non\-interactively here, it cannot prompt to accept an unknown host key.
.SS Capabilities
.CS
list stat get put delete mkdir move
.CE
.PP
\fBcopy\fR is \fBnot\fR reported: SFTP has no server\-side copy. Copying a file is done at the application level with get+put (a cross\-provider copy does exactly this). \fBmove\fR maps to sftp's \fBrename\fR.
.PP
\fBhead\fR is \fBnot\fR a cap. It inherits \fBBase\fR (\fBget\fR then truncate). Measured 2026\-09\-23: OpenSSH \fBsftp get\fR is \fBget [\-afpR] remote [local]\fR — no offset, no length. A prefix preview still downloads the whole file. Do not advertise a partial fetch the client cannot do.
.SS Operations
.IP \(bu
\fBlist $path\fR \-\- runs \fBls \-l $path\fR over sftp and parses the Unix long listing. sftp prints the full path in the name column, so the leaf is taken with \fBfile tail\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBstat $path\fR \-\- sftp's \fBls\fR has no \fB\-d\fR, so stat lists the PARENT directory and picks the matching entry (root \fB/\fR is reported as a directory).
.IP \(bu
\fBget\fR / \fBput\fR \-\- transfer via a local temp file (sftp works on paths, not in\-memory data), read/written back as bytes.
.IP \(bu
\fBdelete\fR \-\- tries \fBrm\fR, falls back to \fBrmdir\fR for directories.
.IP \(bu
\fBmkdir\fR / \fBmove\fR \-\- forward to sftp's \fBmkdir\fR / \fBrename\fR.
.SS "Notes and limits"
.IP \(bu
\fBWhole\-file transfers.\fR Plain sftp transfers whole files. \fBhead\fR uses the base default (get + truncate). OpenSSH has no range\-get in batch mode.
.IP \(bu
\fBls \-l\fR\fB format.\fR The common Unix long listing is assumed. The link\-count column may be \fB?\fR on some servers; only the perms (field 1), size (field 5) and name (field 9+) columns are used, so that is fine.
.IP \(bu
\fBOne process per operation.\fR Each call spawns an sftp process. Fine for interactive browsing; a batch of many small operations pays per\-call startup.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtuprovider\fR, \fBtuprovider::ftp\fR, \fBtuprovider::dav\fR, \fBtuprovider::zip\fR
